Legal and Compliance Counsel	"About the job
Position Snapshot 

Location: Singapore, Eightrium

Company: Nestlé Singapore

Permanent – Full Time

3 to 5 years of relevant working experience in a good law firm/established company.

Position Summary

Joining Nestlé means you are joining the largest Food and Beverage Company in the world. At our very core, we are a human environment – passionate people driven by the purpose of enhancing the quality of life and contributing to a healthier future. A Nestle career empowers you to make an impact locally and globally, as you are provided with the opportunity to make a mark and stand out, as long as you seek it. With Nestle, you are enabled and encouraged to grow not only as professionals, but also as people.

We are looking for a Legal & Compliance Advisor to provide legal and compliance advice and to partner the business to provide solutions to issues while managing legal and compliance risks, including data protection, competition law, anti-corruption, consumer pprotection, sanctions.

A day in the life of a Legal & Compliance Advisor...

Provide prompt and competent support to Director, Legal to enable Legal to advise and assist the business
Reviews, designs, proposes, implements, and/or audits data protection and privacy matters, practices and documentation (including policies, notices, terms and conditions, etc) for Nestlé in Malaysia/Singapore in compliance with applicable laws and Nestlé policies, and considering the Nestlé business needs.
Works with legal team and functional/business data protection champions to ensure that businesses collects and processes personal data in a compliant manner in accordance with Nestlé standards policies, guidelines.
Be familiar with and knowledgeable on the latest developments in data protection generally and in particular in MY/SG as well as the Nestlé Data Protection Office. Create awareness by producing and conducting training and other awareness activities. Ensure that the data register, consent registers and all other requirements are up to date and compliant.
To work closely with the IT department and HQ Compliance to ensure that any privacy assessments, including privacy impact assessment/business impact assessment, vendor assessments are structured and conducted in accordance with Nestlé standards and applicable laws.
Day-to-day administrative support and maintenance of legal framework and matters
Drafting and preparation of contracts, documents, letters, communications, training materials
Keeps updated on legal developments and constantly reviews documents and policies to ensure compliance.
Ensure legal advice is accurate by performing relevant reseach and ensure proper contract management systems are in place.
Reviews and advises on Intellectual Property issues and matters, and manages access to IP databases.
Manages and drives projects independently to achieve desired results.

What Will Make You Successful...

A good degree from a recognized university and being called to the bar in a commonwealth jurisdiction similar to Singapore’s legal system would be an advantage.
Preferably has data protection background experience for Singapore. Competition law, GDPR and IT knowledge is a bonus.
Preferably at least 3 to 5 years PQE or relevant working experience in a good law firm/established company.
Relevant FMCG experience would be an advantage"
